	...sort of.  Problem is, I never even got the chance to die.  I'm
playing 3.0j and doing PDG (that's Pretty Damn Good) when I realize, Hey, I'm
missing one of my favorite TV shows.  So I save the game, but not wanting to
log out, I type:
(sleep 600; nethack)&
so that in another 10 minutes (that's how much longer the show had to go) it
would just start up my saved game of nethack automatically.  Right?  Wrong!
It turns out, the process managed to completely wipe out the saved game, and
I find myself starting anew.  Normally, I don't even have access to the save
files.  WAAAAA!!!
	So the moral of the story, kiddies, is that putting your game of net-
hack to sleep is more akin to putting your dog to sleep.  So don't do it.
